chosen:
Kokuyō (concept 1) is the winner. Below, "A" means concept 1 (Kokuyō) and "B" means concept 2 (Ayatsuri). I fixed four of its flaws:
- one "go" moment 0.36 s before every impact, instead of A's 0.425 s;
- a camera profile for this boss that measurably fits him on screen, plus a cap on how tall his poses get;
- a violet shadow with a "hole" of light around Kaito, so a black-clad Kaito never stands on black;
- an Act 3 eclipse that stays playable after the night-visibility fix.

From Ayatsuri (B) I grafted:
- the readability contract: the warning cue is timed off seconds-to-impact (strikeEta), tracking locks at the cue, and unblockables get a two-beat warning;
- a punish window that hits don't drain;
- abilities that interrupt only before the cue;
- a safe core for his sweep;
- a boss that visibly comes apart as the fight goes on;
- warning sounds pitched by attack type;
- the pale-floor evidence;
- the cp_dojo relocation;
- the phaseDuration and phaseBark hooks;
- a finisher camera scaled to the target's height;
- the scythe-ribbon lore hook, made to fit the bandana story that already ships.
